       The  program  below  provide  subset  of  the  functionality of the rree‐‐
       qquueesstt--kkeeyy(8) program provided by the _k_e_y_u_t_i_l_s  package.   For  informa‐
       tional purposes, the program records various information in a log file.

       As  described  in rreeqquueesstt__kkeeyy(2), the rreeqquueesstt--kkeeyy(8) program is invoked
       with command‐line arguments that describe a key that is to be instanti‐
       ated.  The example program fetches and logs these arguments.  The  pro‐
       gram  assumes  authority to instantiate the requested key, and then in‐
       stantiates that key.

       The following shell session demonstrates the use of this  program.   In
       the  session, we compile the program and then use it to temporarily re‐
       place the standard rreeqquueesstt--kkeeyy(8) program.  (Note that temporarily dis‐
       abling the standard rreeqquueesstt--kkeeyy(8) program may not be safe on some sys‐
       tems.)  While our example program is installed, we use the example pro‐
       gram shown in rreeqquueesstt__kkeeyy(2) to request a key.

           $ cccc --oo kkeeyy__iinnssttaannttiiaattee kkeeyy__iinnssttaannttiiaattee..cc --llkkeeyyuuttiillss;
           $ ssuuddoo mmvv //ssbbiinn//rreeqquueesstt--kkeeyy //ssbbiinn//rreeqquueesstt--kkeeyy..bbaacckkuupp;
           $ ssuuddoo ccpp kkeeyy__iinnssttaannttiiaattee //ssbbiinn//rreeqquueesstt--kkeeyy;
           $ ..//tt__rreeqquueesstt__kkeeyy uusseerr mmyykkeeyy ssoommeeppaayyllooaaddddaattaa;
           Key ID is 20d035bf
           $ ssuuddoo mmvv //ssbbiinn//rreeqquueesstt--kkeeyy..bbaacckkuupp //ssbbiinn//rreeqquueesstt--kkeeyy;

